    "reading_order": 12,
    "text": "1. An event having only one outcome of the experiment is called an elementary\nevent. In Example 1, both the events E and F are elementary events. Similarly, in\nExample 2, all the three events, Y, B and R are elementary events.",
    "latex": null,
    "image_ref": null,
