      437.99
    ],
    "reading_order": 17,
    "text": "Solution : (i) Here, let E be the event ‘getting a number greater than 4’. The number\nof possible outcomes is six : 1, 2, 3, 4, 5 and 6, and the outcomes favourable to E are 5\nand 6. Therefore, the number of outcomes favourable to E is 2. So,",
